2.11. Internal Oscillator (OSCE)
An internal programmable rate oscillator is provided on all Avant devices. The oscillator can be used for FPGA configuration,
system monitoring/ATM (Anti-Tampering Monitor) block, and as a user logic clock source that is available after FPGA
configuration. There is one OSCE on the Avant device. The oscillator clock output is routed directly to primary clocking.
The oscillator output is not a high-accuracy clock, having a +/- 10% variation in its output frequency. It is mainly used for
circuits that do not require a high degree of clock accuracy.

